'c' is a mistake.]V[-2.7]SBKV[24.64];W[qe]LB[mb:a][rb:b]MA[qe]C[Black continues with 'a' or 'b'.
With 'a' he aims for the top side, with 'b' he tries to take the right side, but cannot force White to give it.]V[-2.8](;B[mb];W[ne];B[md]LB[rb:E][oe:A][nf:C][of:D][ng:B]MA[md]C[* Joseki *

The sequence is joseki because White has sente.
White has no influence, because Black has continuations on 'a' and 'b'.
White center continuations on 'c' or 'd' are more urgent than the endgame on 'e'.
